@osuki-dev/ui 2.0.0-beta.0 (Android): Text puts the trailing slack inside the
fontVariationSettings run, so the thin space is drawn at the run's axes and its
advance follows the requested weight. A centred label in a variable reader
face (wght != the face's default) moved by a point against 1.x, where the app
appended the slack after the run, at the paragraph's own face.

Fix: when the run is split off, append the slack after the run instead of
inside it. Remove when the kit ships the same placement (beta.1 changeset:
"Text keeps the hug slack outside the variation run").

